  "paper_diagnosis": "Fulminant Hepatic Failure in Dengue Fever Without Plasma Leakage",
  "disease_label_per_paper": "Dengue fever complicated by fulminant hepatic failure and fatal hemorrhage without plasma leakage",
  "expected_manifold": "D-DENGUE",
  "demographics": {
    "age": 16,
    "sex": "M"
  },
  "presentation_summary": [
    "16-year-old Sri Lankan boy presented with 3 days of high fever, myalgia, arthralgia, and retro-orbital pain.",
    "He had no mucocutaneous bleeding, no respiratory infection features, no rash, no lymphadenopathy, no prior dengue, and no history of hepatotoxic drug or alcohol exposure.",
    "At admission he was afebrile, conscious and rational, blood pressure 130/80 mmHg, heart rate 88/min, with no postural drop, no tachycardia, and no plasma leakage.",
    "Admission blood count showed leukopenia and thrombocytopenia with WBC 3.0 x10^9/L, hematocrit 43.1%, hemoglobin 14.3 g/dL, and platelets 90 x10^9/L; initial liver and renal functions were normal.",
    "Dengue NS1 antigen was positive on illness day 4.",
    "Thirty-six hours later he became restless with platelets 27 x10^9/L, AST 1080 U/L, ALT 546 U/L, INR 3.45, lactate 4 mmol/L, and pH 7.3; ultrasound still showed no plasma leakage.",
    "He received acute liver failure care including N-acetylcysteine, methylprednisolone, intubation, plasma exchange, FFP, and cryoprecipitate, but later developed intraventricular, gastrointestinal, and pulmonary hemorrhage and died."
  ],
